# A finding under a list spread names the WRONG element, because the
# reference's copy shared the close() call's inner map with every
# other element and each rebased its path in turn. Run:
#   aontu vet refarg-list-index.aontu refarg-list-index.json
# Two bad elements with a good one between them is what tells the
# three answers apart: TypeScript reported the FIRST element's path
# for both findings, Go the LAST element's, and only a copy that owns
# its arguments reports each element at its own index.
# expected: findings at $.l.0.e and $.l.2.e
# actual:   both at $.l.2.e (Go) / both at $.l.0.e (TypeScript)
# FIXED 2026-09-07 (ADR-025).
E: hide(re("^g$"))
ent: { U: close({ e: $.E }) }
ent: hide({})
l: [&: $.ent.U]
